    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (only `AcceptanceTest` exists, and it passes, as does a targeted run).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of existing owners sharing the new owner's first and last name (case-insensitively), captured at create time \u2014 following the existing derived-field pattern (`customerCode`, `householdId`).\n\nChanges:\n- **`CountNamesakes`** (new function, `rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 mirrors `AssignCustomerCode`: iterates `ownerRepository.findAll()`, counting case-insensitive first+last-name matches, and stamps the built `Owner` in place. Runs before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner is excluded from its own count.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `countNamesakes` step (under the `transaction` governance) between `assignHousehold` and `save`.\n- **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the `namesakeCount` field (`namesake_count` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` (int32, min 0) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and the existing MapStruct `toOwnerDto` maps it by name automatically.\n- **Schema files** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe responsibility stays isolated in its own single-purpose function; no existing class absorbed unrelated logic, and the mapping reuses the auto-generated DTO plumbing rather than adding a hand-written mapping.",
